  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Content addressing",
      "items": [
        "Chunks and internal nodes are both addressed by hash",
        "Upload is bottom-up: children must exist before the parent",
        "If the root hash exists, the whole tree is present"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "One MMR per bucket",
      "items": [
        "Append adds a leaf; freeze locks start_seq",
        "Delete: a new MMR starts at the current end (start_seq + leaf_count); the kept leaves are appended again with new sequence numbers",
        "Canonical range: [start_seq, start_seq + leaf_count); an append checkpoint proves the old MMR is a prefix (MmrConsistencyProof)",
        "Non-canonical [A, A+N) is prunable once canonical [B, B+M) has B+M > A+N"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Signed CommitmentPayload",
      "items": [
        "CommitmentPayload { version (2), genesis_hash, bucket_id, agreement_id, commitment }; BucketId is a u64 newtype, AgreementId a u32 newtype",
        "genesis_hash is in the signed preimage only: it is never transmitted, the chain reconstructs it with its own genesis hash, so a signature verifies on one chain only",
        "agreement_id binds the commitment to one agreement; when that agreement ends, the commitment is void"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What a proof must show",
      "items": [
        "chunk_proof (MerkleProof): the chunk is in the leaf's data_root",
        "mmr_proof (MmrProof): peaks, leaf and leaf_proof to the mmr_root",
        "If either check fails, the response is rejected with InvalidProof and the challenge stays open",
        "Every proof list is bounded: at most 64 tree levels and 64 MMR peaks (MaxProofDepth)"
      ]
    }
  ]
